Boolean-based Inference Attack
Attack Principle: When application doesn't display data but has differential responses, infer data bit by bit through true/false conditions
Feature Detection:
Multiple AND-connected conditions:
Complex conditional expressions connected by multiple ANDs
Length detection functions:
LENGTH(...), CHAR_LENGTH(...)
Used to detect field or query result length
Character extraction functions:
SUBSTRING(str, pos, len), SUBSTR(...)
MID(str, pos, len)
LEFT(str, len), RIGHT(str, len)
Character encoding conversion:
ASCII(...), ORD(...): character to ASCII code
HEX(...): hexadecimal encoding
BIN(...): binary encoding
Bit-by-bit comparison:
SUBSTRING(password,1,1)='a'
ASCII(SUBSTRING(username,2,1))>97
Multi-layer nested structures:
Nested subqueries obscuring core logic
Complex conditional judgment chains
Judgment Points:
Whether character-by-character/bit-by-bit extraction and comparison patterns exist
Whether complexity of conditional expressions is abnormal
Whether attempting to infer hidden information